{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1281000-help-with-custom-legacy-the-nizari","id":1281000,"title":"Help with Custom Legacy - The Nizari","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-15T16:09:57-08:00","id":1281000,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Help with Custom Legacy - The Nizari","content":"Hello<br /> <br /> So, I'm trying to make a new legacy but some of the rules I can't get my head around when trying to make new attaiments not to mention how do we get access to them, do I need to meet the gnosis requirement to unlock them or just the arcana, both? as you can see I'm kind of new to the Mage game, took it to learn to play, anyway<br /> <br /> The Legacy is based on the actual Nizari Ismailis, long story short, they are the Assassins of old, the real deal according to wikipedia (It's the internet, it can't lie to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) Link <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassins\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> So far with the help from people here this is what came out.<br /> <br /> Also credit where credit is due, kudos and thanks to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\">KaiserAfini</a> for coming up with the attaiments. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Legacy: The Nizari</b></span></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Origins</b></span> <span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Parentage</b></span></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Path:</span></b> Mastigos</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Order:</span></b> Guardian of the Veil</span></span></span></span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Concept:</span></b> Assassins</span></span></span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Appearance: </span></b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Nizari </span></span></span></span>are encouraged to not make many waves, in their mundane lives they could be just about anybody, they many faces and backgrounds, quite a few of those are actually fabricated, they make heavy use of their masques to have several background ready for what a job would require.<br /> <br /> They only recruit from members of the order, those that show a great level of dedicaion and self sacrifice draw their attention and the very exigences from the order cull those that wouldn't be a good fit.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Background:</span> </b>The Nizari Fidai are what the old order of assassins was called, dated back to the 11th century days they were born in what is now the ruined Alamut fortress on the South Caspian province of Gilan near the Rudbar region in Iran, lead by a mystierious &quot;Old man of the mountain&quot; they were a political and religious faction of Shia Islam, or so history would have you believe, in reality they were a sect of Guardians that during their time used the political and religious turmoil of the era to further their secret agenda.<br /> <br /> Much of the legacy's past was lost with the destruction of their forstresses and the burning of the library of Alamut, when they were invaded by the Mongol Empire during the invasion of Khwarism or so they would have you believe in reality they orchestated their own fall to cover the legacy in another layer of secrecy and so they could spread their numbers further accross the world, somethings are commonly known about the order though, it's founder was a Guardian Epoch of the Mastgos Path, Hassan-i Sabbah responsible for the widespread nature on the middle east, though only a limited group of Nizari were actually awakened members of the legacy. He saw and suffered under the regime of the Seers of the Throne that manipulated events to steal the reign of the Caliph orchestating a coup and putting one of their own in the throne, captured for a time he took the opportnity to meditate and plan in his prison waiting and bidding his time untilt the moment was right to act, he was changed by the experience and in his very soul he rejected the Hubris of the Seers, change as he was he founded his movement taking over the fortress of Alamut and spreading from there. He used an army of sleepers to combat the influence of the Seers of the Throne using asymmetrical and psychological warfare and surgical strikes particulary their assassinations of key individuals.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">And for the better part of three centuries they were a force to be reckon with, having succefully assassinated key figures across their early history, two known Caliphs, many viziers, sultans and crusader leaders.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Nowadays the legacy no longer subscribes to a particular set of beliefs religious or otherwise, you can see traces of them among the history of the world, the cold war was basically their playground, in more modern settings they can be easily found as part of black ops teams in any miliatry or as hitmen among the criminal underworld, some venerate the Santa Muerte in the mexicans cartels, so work in any of the soup letter intelligence agencies across the world, their background may vary, though their purpose and MO remain the same.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3366ff\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Prerequisites: </span></b></span>Gnosis 2, Death 2, Status 2 Guardian of the Veil and at least one mastered Masque.</span></span></span></span><ul><li><b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Thesis:</span></b> It is the nature of the Diamond Wheel to advance, refining all souls while flattening the trail for the arrival the Hieromagus, who shall redeem all sins and reclaim the Imperium Mysteriorum for mankind. The Exarchs would chain its movements so this does not come to pass.<br /> <br /> But there is one Truth they forget: All things contain shatterpoints, precise locations that can be stricken to utterly destroy them. So too does destiny, for a simple phrase or speech can change the course of history or an army can be rendered ineffective by the death of few key figures. For the chosen few, even the fetters of the Tyrants can become evident. See the chains of the lie, become the blade that will sever its weakest link and allow the Diamond Wheel to turn unhindered.</li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Organization: </span></b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The unifying doctrine of the Nizari is their dedication to their cause, what is their cause changes from Caucus from Caucus, but some things remain constant, they are never the ones leading, they can hold authority over others, but never are they the leader or heriarchs on the concilium, they are followers, very dedicated followers, but just followers in the end, if such would take such lofty ambision for himself it better be on a temporary manner and setting the stage for a proper leader to replace him one way or another or he would see himself eventually culled from the ranks of the Legacy. No, the Nizari themselves don't rule, they are the power behind the throne others are the sword and shield of the Pentacle orders, the Nizari are happy to be their silent blade in the night.<br /> <br /> There is a reason for this though, a Nizari for the most part try to avoid the trappings of hubris and one of the easier ones to fall comes from sitting in positions of power so they limit themselves this way, there is also the belief that they are just paving their mythical messiah, the Heriomage who they will submit under for judegement of their dedication to its cause, the unfaithful would be cast aside while the steadfast and loyal will be recieved with open arms, finally having sanction from above actually empowers them in their missions allowing them to carry out their assassinations wihtout risking their wisdom in the act.<br /> <br /> They work within the order, they are Guardians of the Veil first and they follow the orders traditions and practices, they make it to the rank os Susceptors most of the time where they settle down, there are occassional grand masters in the legacy but their focus is on recruitment and management of the order members in the local caucus under the vigilant eye of the Epoch, they aren't really numerous as they not many have the temperament to dedicate themselves to the levels that the Nizari do.</span></span></span></span></li> <li><b>Initiation: </b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Nizari ritual of initiation is rather straightfoward but by not mean easy, quite the contrary, in fact the prospective Nizari is tested against an impossible task, this test the initiate in their resourcefulness and dedication, he's pretty much set out to fail in a controled scenario, most commonly he is set up against a disguised member of the legacy willing to play the part of a mark, though to prevent misshaps he is not told to kill his target, just to capture it alive wich normaly adds another layer of difficulty to the task as he's told to do it discreetly and without being caught on the act. The mark is prepared for this and stacks the deck against the prospective new member, occasionaly with his mentor help in a way that is made sure to mess up his plan, how he reacts and adapts under this circumstances makes or breaks the prospective Nizari, though if he actually succeeds against all odds he's quickly inducted into the Legacy.</span></span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Ruling Arcana</span></b></span><br /> Death<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#cccccc\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><b><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Optional Arcana</span></span></b></b></span></span><br /> Space<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Yantras</span></b></span><br /> Detailed files about a Mark (+1), Having been Sanctioned to act by a superior (+2), Tool or weapons of assassination (+1), Using stimulants to keep focused (+1, +2 if a negative condition is caused), While in the presence of their mark and undetected (+1)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Oblations</span></b></span><br /> Studying a target's life, a long session of planning a hit, Shadowing a target, Infiltrating a target's social group, meditatiing on why the target needs to die, announcing the intent to kill the target while explaining why he is going to die.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Attainments</span></b><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">First Attainment: Deadly Sanction/Detached Presence</span></b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 1</span></span></span><ul><li>Spend a scene building a writ of sanctioned assassination for the target, requiring a representational yantra and some data on them. This grants the assassin and any that have signed their names on the writ the Sanctioned condition, useable only for actions to kill the target. If the writ is destroyed, the Condition goes away.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Sanctioned:</b></span> The character enjoys a <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">+2 </span></span>to all mundane actions involving eliminating the target. It can also be resolved to upgrade a mundane action to an Exceptional Success. Lasts as long as the Attainment does, which means master Nizari having up to a year to kill the target , ones with Death 2 having an entire day, Death 3 having a week.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b>Space 1</span></span></span><ul><li>The mission of the Sanctioned demands the utmost focus and dedication with little time for distarctions. After a scene of meditating on the mission, your divine mandate wards you from interference. This applies an inverse variation of Isolation upon yourself or an ally, giving the penalty to any Unsanctioned who try to interact with the beneficiary. You can also apply normal Isolation on a target. Any Sanctioned can interact with them normally, but its a two way street.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Second Attainment: Deadly Silence/Reaching Hands</span></b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 2</span></span></span><ul><li>When Death comes only silence an still are left in it's wake, the Nizari embody this, for after their passing their victims are forever silent . This attainment renders a target (the Nizari, the victim, the murder weapon, etc) completely silent. Reach is assigned to instant use and advanced duration.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b>Space 2</span></span></span><ul><li>There is no place safe from the reaching hands of the Nizari, they will carry out their mission. All of your Legacy Attainments can now be used with Sympathetic Range.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Third Attainment: Death's Touch/Hidden Armory</span></b><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 3</span></span></span><ul><li>There is no impentrable fortress, all have a breaching point and a vulnerable wall, with his attainment the Nizari can even turn it into a tomb for his target, it also good for disposal of evidence, like a targets corpse and murder weapons. As the Decay spell with [Death] potency and Reach assigned to instant use and Structural damage.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b>Space 3</span></span></span><ul><li>Physics tells us that no two objects can occupy the same space, but such things cannot get in the way of an assassin's divine mission. After a scene of preparing to go out on the field, they can link objects together, allowing one to exist at a time while the other is in a &quot;pocket dimension&quot;. Swapping between them is a reflexive action. So a pen can be used to smuggle a gun in, a ring can become a knife or a trusted friend can unknowingly be a time bomb. Up to [Space] pairs of objects can be linked at a time.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Fourth Attainment: Mantle of Darkness/Garrote of the Heart</span></b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 4</span></span></span><ul><li>Just as silence if the voice of the Nizari, darkness is his home, this attainment combines Deepen Shadows and Without a Trace that allows up to 5 Sanctioned see normally within the shadows, and to be affected by Without a Trace for the Duration. Any Unsanctioned who use supernatural effects to try see within provoke a Clash of Wills, earning [Death] automatic successes for the assassin. Reach are spent on Instant Use, Advanced Scale and Advanced Duration.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b>Space 4</span></span></span><ul><li>At this level, the Nizari can turn the most steadfast of friends into a vicious enemy, manipulating those ties to his advantage, after all, who better to strike at the heart than those closes to it. This attainemt twists the nature of sympathetic links, but not the strength. So a person's link to their spouse could go from &quot;love&quot; to &quot;violent repulsion&quot;. Had you borrowed the &quot;love&quot; link, you could alter it to &quot;trusted confidant&quot;. Or even alter the link one has to a pet from &quot;loyal friend&quot; to &quot;pathological fear&quot;. Reach is assigned to instant use and advanced duration.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Fifth Attainment: Weight of Souls/Umbral Paths</span></b><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 5</span></span></span><ul><li>The Nizari dedication carries them on even in the face of death, with this attaiment he spends 1 mana while creating the writ, this creates a stronger connection between the Nizari and his target, if the Nizari mage dies before killing his target his soul doens't depart inmediatly but lingers back to the writ after a time as a Rank 2 ghost in twilight with maximun stats for this level, numina determinated when this attainment is obtained, Influences: Killing, mana instead of essence and finally the ability to jump between sympathetic connections by spending 1 point of mana.<br /> The writ becomes the Nizari ghosts anchor to this world if it is destroyed the Nizari souls departs (He can also be destroyed like a normal ghost like this), but if the target dies before the writ expires or is destroyed the writ is consumed and Nizari revives where it is.The writ gains a peculiarity however, it starts to whisper in ghostly voices everything that the Nizari sees. (Reach is used for Advanced Duration)</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b>Optional Arcana: </b></span></span></span>Space 5</span></span></span><ul><li>The master Nizari is a slippery inividual by his his own skills alone, with this attainment however he's the boogyman to his targets, striking one second and cleanly slipping away the next. As the Teleportation spell with Reach assigned to instant use.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 03-17-2019, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T16:46:04-08:00","id":1281008,"title":"","content":"It requires both Gnosis and Arcana. If your character is creating it themselves, it requires Gnosis 3 and Legacy Arcanum 2. If its an already established Legacy setting wise, it requires Gnosis 2 and Arcanum 2.<br /> <br /> Your character will require the same main/optional Arcanum rating as the Attainment number (plus the needed Gnosis, which varies based on the Attainment), 1 dot for 1st, 4 for 4th and so on.<br /> <br /> To help flesh out the Legacy, you need to come up with their habits. Why did they choose to specialize like this ? How do they pass these teachings down? How are they initiated ? How does this connect to their mage lives ? <br /> <br /> How does an elder Nizari act ? What tools does he use ? Those can help inspire yantras and oblations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-16-2019, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:54:05-08:00","id":1283353,"title":"","content":"The more I try to come up with some of those things the more I trouble I have to make the legacy a thing, I mean, if I take what the actual Nizari were, you could put them side by side with the Guardians of the Veil and end up with the something way too similar, hell you could say that Hasan-i-Sabah was one of the most renowed Guardians in his fortress in Alamut, an Epoch renowed both by mage society and the mundane one...or one hell of a scary Seer of the Throne. As much as I try to make the Legacy unique I just can't find how to divert it from what the Guardians do, Psychological and Asymetrical Warfare plus spy work and assassinations are some of the thing that the Guardians do already, not the whole thing but quite a lot, the most I could come with is an ancient Caucus not a legacy.<br /> <br /> Or am I reading the order wrong?<br /> <br /> Maybe if I explain where do the idea comes from you guys might be able to point me in the right direction, I just to bounce ideas with the community I guess.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Legacy comes in response to a setting, picture this, the seers won, you lost the city to them, hell, there won even on the magic department, they somehow manage to put a spell on the city that targets everybody that is not a Seer, if you ever over reach with magic you get hit by paradox twice as hard as your normally would, add to that your magic is also crippled, you can't go above certain potency cap, you can try and the spell might still hit but its not as potent.<br /> <br /> The concilium is a mere shadow of what it once was, the law and pretty much the need of the concilium is secrecy, you cant afford to be discovered, prime material for a cold war were you are the underdog, the hidden militia, etc.<br /> <br /> I kind of know what I want I just can't grasp it, I have trouble building it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T15:19:31-08:00","id":1283372,"title":"","content":"Is there a problem with a legacy that manages to perfectly embody the ideals of an Order? Maybe instead of fighting it, embrace it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T18:17:19-08:00","id":1284427,"title":"","content":"Its not a bad thing to be resonant with the Order, it can be a lens to examine its diferent facets. For example, the Bearers of the Eternal Voice examine the Guardians as the masters of cleaning up breaches of the Veil. At their best, they can help cover up a big blunder or throw Sleepers off the cabal's trail. At their worst they are poker faced liars that can censor even your memories, driving paranoia up for everybody.<br /> <br /> The Subtle Ones represent them as an invisible hand, shadow manipulators. They have a great number of agencies, who in turn operate other agencies. Boxes stacked one in another. They shut down or reactivate them as needed, but they never touch anything directly. They only influence. Suggest. Insinuate.<br /> <br /> The Eleventh Question are the Guardians that know that being able to quickly investigate a situation can be vital to prevent catastrophic damage to the Veil, even if it means becoming instruments of revelation rather than occlusion.<br /> <br /> What facet of the Guardians do the Nizari represent? How are they different in approach and motivation from, for example, the Thread Cutters ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T16:08:56-08:00","id":1285071,"title":"","content":"Thread Cutters, to me at least, are more dedicated to the prophetic aspect, if they kill it's because they see that the targets life thread should be cut because of their beliefs and that the fate of their target is a bad one or something like that.<br /> <br /> The Nizari might be similar, but rather than do so because they read a person fate, they do so as part of a mission, The Nizari would be men and women fully dedicated to the cause, I'm trying to make them particulary good Susceptors, they are like independant agents of the GoV, the ones you send to infiltrate a enemy stronghold, take out a target, then walk out without people noticing anything wrong until it's too late, basically these are the Hitmens of the GoV.<br /> <br /> They can be extremists and fanatical killers fully believing they are doing what they do for a great cause, it makes them dedicated at best, uhinged and callous at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 02-05-2019, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T16:30:57-08:00","id":1285075,"title":"","content":"Just to confirm, is Prime necessarily set as the main Arcanum ? Are you working on it pre-campaign or do you already have a Mastigos investing in Prime ? Because the first idea that appeared my head for an assassin Legacy is to have Death. Shadows, cold, entropy, silence, it allows you to cloak your Nimbus, kill spells, fake death, reverse wounds with Unmaking, control the consequences of the kill or just rot the evidence away.<br /> <br /> The second idea was to make Space the optional Arcanum and use the Obtenebrate Discipline from Vampire: The Masquerade to inspire the Attainments, but giving them a remote casting component.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-05-2019, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T16:11:49-08:00","id":1285419,"title":"","content":"I already have a Mastigos invested with Prime, yes, as for the Obtenebrate Discipline I don't know anything about that, never played the old World of Darkness, much less vampire other than the PC games.<br /> <br /> I'm open to hear ideas on what you had in mind though, and as for why I went with Prime I mostly saw it as a tool for the mage, it does the cloaking from spells too, might be used to get around another mage magic regardless of Arcana and can blur the trails of his own magic, I was going to supplement it with Mind instead of Space, but I'm open to suggestions as I said before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T18:23:21-08:00","id":1285449,"title":"","content":"Here is what I have so far. Its a first draft, so its very rough:<br /> <br /> Death 1: Spend a scene building a writ of sanctioned assassination for the target, requiring a representational yantra and some data on them. This grants the assassin a variation of the Informed condition, useable only for actions to kill the target. If the writ is destroyed, the Condition goes away.<br /> <br /> Observation: To avoid repetition, I will use the term Sanctioned, which means any Legacy members. Furthermore, anyone who signed the writ specific to the target (cabal mates, enemies, etc) is considered Sanctioned only for that target, but if the writ is destroyed, they are no longer Sanctioned.<br /> <br /> Space 1: After a scene of meditating on the mission, your divine mandate wards you from interference. This applies an inverse variation of Isolation upon yourself or an ally, giving the penalty to any Unsanctioned who try to interact with the beneficiary. <br /> <br /> You can also apply normal Isolation on a target. Any Sanctioned can interact with them normally, but its a two way street.<br /> <br /> Death 2: Renders a target (the Nizari, the victim, the murder weapon, etc) completely silent. Reach is assigned to instant use and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> Space 2: All your Attainments can now be used with Sympathetic Range. This opens up a lot of shenanigans, especially with the higher Attainments.<br /> <br /> Death 3: Decay with [Death] potency and Reach assigned to instant use and Structural damage. So lets say you use UV paint to mark key points of a building the target will be in with High Speech runes, or ectoplasm or any other clever method. Now you can collapse it while being very far away. Its also practical for dissolving the corpse to leave no evidence.<br /> <br /> Space 3: Physics tells us that no two objects can occupy the same space, but such things cannot get in the way of an assassin's divine mission. After a scene of preparing to go out on the field, they can link objects together, allowing one to exist at a time while the other is in a &quot;pocket dimension&quot;. Swapping between them is a reflexive action. So a pen can be used to smuggle a gun in, a ring can become a knife or a trusted friend can unknowingly be a time bomb. Up to [Space] pairs of objects can be linked at a time.<br /> <br /> Death 4: A variation of Deepen Shadows that lets anyone Sanctioned see normally. Any Unsanctioned who use supernatural effects to try see within provoke a Clash of Wills, earning [Death] automatic successes for the assassin. Reach is assigned to instant use, advanced scale, advanced duration and causing the Blind tilt.<br /> <br /> Space 4: Twists the nature of sympathetic links, but not the strength. So a person's link to their spouse could go from &quot;love&quot; to &quot;violent repulsion&quot;. Had you borrowed the &quot;love&quot; link, you could alter it to &quot;trusted confidant&quot;. Or even alter the link one has to a pet from &quot;loyal friend&quot; to &quot;pathological fear&quot;. Reach is assigned to instant use and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> Death 5: Spend a mana to kill all Unsanctioned supernatural effects in the area (not sure what could be used for the Withstand rating). Reach is used on instant use and mana is spent on activating Everywhere.<br /> <br /> Space 5: Teleportation with Reach assigned to instant use. Its an entry route, escape option, an excellent way to have battlefield mobility, end pursuits instantly and a way to kill your target by teleporting them into the sun, all packed into one.<br /> <br /> <br /> I tried to come up with Attainments that could be useful to the Nizari without removing the challenge of the assassination. At least not until the last ones, because by the time they reach the peak, they need to feel like masters of their art. It might also be a good idea to collapse all the ritual duration ones so they can be all executed using one scene, just to keep the game flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-06-2019, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T09:20:43-08:00","id":1286467,"title":"","content":"That thing about the first death attaiment, the Sacntioned condition, it's a really good idea, it never crossed my mind to add something like that. If we run with that we could use something like a contract for a yantra that is made when then Sanctioned are given a target to kill, for the full bonus a condition like Obsession could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 02-10-2019, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T09:54:57-08:00","id":1286476,"title":"","content":"Its based on the Morag Tong of Morrowind, they embody the honor bound assassin well. The writ is a lens for them to perceive the easiest mundane path to entropy, the honorable assassins getting a boon from the universe, so to speak. <br /> <br /> Mechanically, its a way to avoid lone wolf appoaches while also providing an interesting weakness.<br /> <br /> The attainments are less based on being discrete and more on being terrifying. Mages who know the Nizari are good at hiding can still dimension them as a quantifiable threat. <br /> <br /> But these attainments mean no crowd hinders them, people unconsciously move out of the way. You cannot run from them, bodyguards cannot even touch them. They can darken the stage in the middle of a live speech and teleport the target into the sun. Every place the target steps into could be a deathtrap, every ally could betray them. They can kill with a rocket launcher without anyone hearing or stab them without giving a chance to hear their approach, they can teleport en masse in the shroud of darkness and silently massacre an entire HQ, betraying no clues as to what they are doing.<br /> <br /> Worst still, temporal senses will just see darkness, how can the target even be sure they are fighting humans ? If the Nizari pre-casts Suppress Nimbus and Forge No Chains, there is zero evidence left. When the deed is done, they can reflexively hide their gear or dispose of it with a touch.<br /> <br /> I visualized something like the Terra vs Teen Titans shadow battle or Tosen's Bankai. A mage that is terrified makes bad decisions, their Imagos are less precise.<br /> <br /> Remember the silence and darkness attainments use no spell control and can last up to a year. The Nizari can use them to put an entire city under a siege of darkness, without inconveniencing their allies. What can the Seers, the Left-Handed and Banishers do when there is nowhere to run ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-10-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T11:08:22-08:00","id":1286496,"title":"","content":"The Informed Condition is good only once, using it resolves it. I'd suggest going with a version of Connected instead which is automatically ended when the contract is complete.<br /> <br /> The Death 2 attainment I don't think can work, Death doesn't have silence as part of its purview, and even if it did that level of power is either Unraveling or Unmaking. <br /> <br /> The fifth attainment could be modeled on Supernal Dispellation. For the Space part you can't teleport a target into the sun without having done the prerequisite prep work<br /> .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T15:29:26-08:00","id":1286554,"title":"","content":"I wasn't sure about silence. Shadows are a manifestation of the Death Arcanum, so manifesting them makes a lot of sense. <br /> <br /> But cold is the death of Forces, which can be manifested independently (even if combining some Forces in would make it need less Death). So I imagined extinguishing sound could be doable, but wasn't sure what practice to use.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the assassins would require doing some setup or otherwise the attainments would be too insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T16:05:12-08:00","id":1286565,"title":"","content":"No such things astoo insane really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T15:26:39-08:00","id":1286869,"title":"","content":"The silence of Death is not appropiate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T15:33:42-08:00","id":1286873,"title":"","content":"It could be, perhaps as an Absence of sound. The Practice would still be higher than the 2 dot mark I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T16:57:02-08:00","id":1286903,"title":"","content":"In actuality, I had all the other attainments penned down, but had no clue what to do for Death 2. So I remembered reading a long time ago that one of the most useful abilities in Quietus (a VTM discipline focused on assassination) was a very early one that created a zone of silence (I think its called Silence of Death).<br /> <br /> After thinking about how it synergizes with the others, it seemed too interesting not to use. I wasn't sure if it fell in Death's purview (without requiring some investment in Forces) or at what level, but at worst it could fall into the &quot;Strange Attainments&quot; clause as something only the Nizari could pull off so easily. It didn't seem game breaking and resonated with the theme, so it felt like a worthwhile addition to their toolkit.<br /> <br /> On a side note, the third Space Attainment doesn't truly use a pocket dimension, its actually a Weaving practice used to create a &quot;Schrodinger's Space&quot; in which the mage can choose what &quot;state&quot; the &quot;cat&quot; is in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-11-2019, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T18:40:54-08:00","id":1286929,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there was a Disciple level Space spell in 1e that did pretty much the same thing. You could probably justify just using Co-Location to pull it off if you wanted. Making the switch then would cost a mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T03:44:07-08:00","id":1287011,"title":"","content":"The Space Attainment sounds much more like Patterning unless you make it like a modified Co-Location and merely swap the location of two objects rather than having two objects occupy the same space. I.e: You have a gun at home and a pen in your hand, and you can reflexively swap them (once per turn due to lack of Reaches) so that you have a pen at home and a gun in your hand. No Mana should be required for the switch, though. Since the Attainment is specialised to only work on pairs (possibly also requiring the objects to have the same Size), I would consider making the duration indefinite which would make casting the Attainment on a pair cost one Mana. Or just have the casting cost one Mana regardless due to it being effectively two swaps per turn and safe from Iris intrusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-12-2019, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T05:06:28-08:00","id":1287024,"title":"","content":"Hi!! I've read the draft made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> , and I'm just in love with his aproach.<br /> <br /> I've been tinkering with a few 2nd edition legacies by now, and one thing I miss from legacies from first edition is the posibility of using, in adition to the main arcanum of the legacy and the optional, a third conjuntional Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Using this, you may solve the problem of silencing your steps or anything related to sound, and integrate a few quirks with the usage of Forces as a Conjuntional Arcanum.<br /> <br /> A first aproximation to the solution, could be something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment</b>:<br /> <b>Death 1</b>: Spend a scene building a writ of sanctioned assassination for the target, requiring a representational yantra and some data on them. This grants the assassin a variation of the Informed condition, useable only for actions to kill the target. If the writ is destroyed, the Condition goes away.<br /> <b>Optional Space 1</b>: After a scene of meditating on the mission, your divine mandate wards you from interference. This applies an inverse variation of Isolation upon yourself or an ally, giving the penalty to any Unsanctioned who try to interact with the beneficiary. You can also apply normal Isolation on a target. Any Sanctioned can interact with them normally, but its a two way street.<br /> <b>Conjuntional Forces 1</b>: If the mage knows Forces 1, the writ might be replicated in digital media, thus protecting it from destruction via backups. You can only mantein a maximum of up to Forces copies of the writ, which can't be restored if destroyed (or deleted) unless you cast the attainment again. Recasting the attainment destroys all previous copies of the writ and they need to be replicated again.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Death 2:</b> Makes the mage's aura to look the same as the aura of a sleeper as per the Supress Aura spell, with reach spent on advanced duration.<br /> <b>Space 2:</b> All your Attainments can now be used with Sympathetic Range. This opens up a lot of shenanigans, especially with the higher Attainments.<br /> <b>Conjuntional Forces 2:</b> If the Mage also knows forces 2, for the duration of the Death attainment, he may silence himself, imposing a penalty to enemies' Perception rolls equal to his Force dots.<br /> <br /> Also, I' would modify the death part of the Fourth Attainment as follows, as I tend to make the Legacies as selfcontained as possible:<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:<br /> Death 4: </b>An attainment that combines Deepen Shadows and Without a Trace that allows up to 5 Sanctioned see normally within the shadows, and to be affected by Without a Trace for the Duration. Any Unsanctioned who use supernatural effects to try see within provoke a Clash of Wills, earning [Death] automatic successes for the assassin. Reach are spent on Instant Use, Advanced Scale and Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope this is helpful!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24776,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","user":"Eleizel","date":". 02-12-2019, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T06:49:02-08:00","id":1287041,"title":"","content":"I'd still go with the (Persistent) Connected Condition instead of Informed since Informed is only good once. Unless you only expect to make 1 roll to do all the things you need to do to pull off an assassination you're going to have to keep making the writ over and over again if you want it to keep benefiting from Informed. Connected would give you +2 to rolls to get the job done represented by resources and information given to you by whoever is taking out the hit, and it can be resolved for an instant Exceptional Success to deliver your killing blow. I'd limit though to being something that someone in the legacy can't create all by themselves, they need someone else to empower them in this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:18:26-08:00","id":1287320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eleizel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1281000-help-with-custom-legacy-the-nizari?p=1287024#post1287024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!! I've read the draft made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> , and I'm just in love with his aproach.<br /> <br /> I've been tinkering with a few 2nd edition legacies by now, and one thing I miss from legacies from first edition is the posibility of using, in adition to the main arcanum of the legacy and the optional, a third conjuntional Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Using this, you may solve the problem of silencing your steps or anything related to sound, and integrate a few quirks with the usage of Forces as a Conjuntional Arcanum.<br /> <br /> A first aproximation to the solution, could be something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment</b>:<br /> <b>Death 1</b>: Spend a scene building a writ of sanctioned assassination for the target, requiring a representational yantra and some data on them. This grants the assassin a variation of the Informed condition, useable only for actions to kill the target. If the writ is destroyed, the Condition goes away.<br /> <b>Optional Space 1</b>: After a scene of meditating on the mission, your divine mandate wards you from interference. This applies an inverse variation of Isolation upon yourself or an ally, giving the penalty to any Unsanctioned who try to interact with the beneficiary. You can also apply normal Isolation on a target. Any Sanctioned can interact with them normally, but its a two way street.<br /> <b>Conjuntional Forces 1</b>: If the mage knows Forces 1, the writ might be replicated in digital media, thus protecting it from destruction via backups. You can only mantein a maximum of up to Forces copies of the writ, which can't be restored if destroyed (or deleted) unless you cast the attainment again. Recasting the attainment destroys all previous copies of the writ and they need to be replicated again.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b><br /> <b>Death 2:</b> Makes the mage's aura to look the same as the aura of a sleeper as per the Supress Aura spell, with reach spent on advanced duration.<br /> <b>Space 2:</b> All your Attainments can now be used with Sympathetic Range. This opens up a lot of shenanigans, especially with the higher Attainments.<br /> <b>Conjuntional Forces 2:</b> If the Mage also knows forces 2, for the duration of the Death attainment, he may silence himself, imposing a penalty to enemies' Perception rolls equal to his Force dots.<br /> <br /> Also, I' would modify the death part of the Fourth Attainment as follows, as I tend to make the Legacies as selfcontained as possible:<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:<br /> Death 4: </b>An attainment that combines Deepen Shadows and Without a Trace that allows up to 5 Sanctioned see normally within the shadows, and to be affected by Without a Trace for the Duration. Any Unsanctioned who use supernatural effects to try see within provoke a Clash of Wills, earning [Death] automatic successes for the assassin. Reach are spent on Instant Use, Advanced Scale and Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope this is helpful!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, glad you liked it \ud83d\ude04<br /> <br /> There is another one I want to write down: The Gardeners of Gilgamesh, a Moros Legacy of fleshcrafters. At their best, they are the doctors of the Awakened, spearheading the creation of new lifeforms to invent new remedies for Sleepers and Awakened alike. They are also the masters of perfected medicines (and poisons). At their worst, they are insane fleshcrafters that hunt down parts in a mad bid for evolution, both of themselves and the bioweapons of the Awakened. Think of them as a mix of the Tzimisce and the Shapers of the Yuuzhan Vong.<br /> <br /> I also have another written down, of enlightened strategists. They focus a lot on Plan equipment and can give a pretty powerful boost to the cabal.<br /> <br /> The conjunctional Force effects are a pretty cool solution, I like it a lot. Suppress Aura synergizes well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-12-2019, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T16:24:23-08:00","id":1287323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1281000-help-with-custom-legacy-the-nizari?p=1287041#post1287041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd still go with the (Persistent) Connected Condition instead of Informed since Informed is only good once. Unless you only expect to make 1 roll to do all the things you need to do to pull off an assassination you're going to have to keep making the writ over and over again if you want it to keep benefiting from Informed. Connected would give you +2 to rolls to get the job done represented by resources and information given to you by whoever is taking out the hit, and it can be resolved for an instant Exceptional Success to deliver your killing blow. I'd limit though to being something that someone in the legacy can't create all by themselves, they need someone else to empower them in this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes me imagine an Interfector or someone similarly empowered by the Lex Magicka having to validate the writ. Connected also sounds more useful and practical than Informed.<br /> <br /> How about the third Attainment using mana for any affected items the Nizari is not touching ? That way sneaking in equipment remains practical but setting off traps is a bit more expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-12-2019, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T23:16:18-08:00","id":1287434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1281000-help-with-custom-legacy-the-nizari?p=1287320#post1287320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gardeners of Gilgamesh, a Moros Legacy of fleshcrafters</div> </div> </div> </div> Man, just the concept seems sick cool. <br /> <br /> Actually... I think I have a few ideas... Probably you want Life has main Arcanum for the Legacy, and I'd go with Death for the optional. A rough draft of the attainment could be like this:<br /> <br /> First Attainment: Analyze Life, Reach for Instant cast.<br /> Optional Death 1: Soul Marks, Reach for Instant cast.<br /> <br /> Second Attainment: Purge Illness, Reach for Instant cast.<br /> Optional Death 2: No fucking idea about this.<br /> <br /> Third Attainment: Transform Life, Reach for Advanced Duration.<br /> Optional Death 3: Ghostly Limbs, This should work somewhat similar to Shape Ephemera but allows the Mage to create a ghostly limb(s) and integrate it into himself or another. It would allow him to interact with both death attuned ephemera and normal matter (as per the touch of the grave) and probably give some minor bonuses depending on the limb (additional arm may grant +1 for fine manipulation while additional legs maybe +1 speed or similar, probably even wings could be possible, but not for full flight, just gliding) Reach for Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> Fourth Attainment: Improved Transform Life, you now may cast the third attainment as an instant action. While affected by the Third Attainment, the target receives the effects of the Body Control spell with ranks equal to half Life dots (rounding up).<br /> Optional Death 4: Rotting Flesh, Reach for Instant Cast and for -3 penalty in social rolls.<br /> <br /> Fifth Attainment: Sublime Transform Life, you may make the changes indefinite by spending 1 mana. This traits are inheritable. <br /> Optional Death 5: Your fourth death attainment now deals Lethal damage. You may impose up to half your death dots (rounding up) physical tilts like arm wrack, leg wrack, poisoned, sick, deafened or blind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T16:10:48-08:00","id":1287729,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24776\" data-vbnamecard=\"24776\">Eleizel</a> Using ectoplasm to create a mold and transforming it into a part of their pattern is a very cool idea, very resonant with the Moros. But I had an idea that was a bit different, the Gardeners use Life as Ruling and Matter as optional. Mechanically, they are an attempt to create a healer Legacy without only focusing on healing spells, mixing in some Tzimisce/Yuuzhang Vong horror into the greater focus on medicine. Thematically, they are the mages that wept at the fates of Gilgamesh and Enkidu (one of their Attainments even reflects this), swearing to do what they could not, in eternal defiance of the Exarchs. They are ancient, recently rediscovered and reintegrated into Pentacle culture by a joint Mysterium-Free Council project, much to the horror of the Guardians.<br /> <br /> Here is the first draft of the Attainments, if there is any interest, I can flesh them out:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Life 1</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Analyze Life, with Reach assigned to instant use. If used to reveal medicinal applications of a living being, it shows all possible uses of every part.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Matter 1</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Craftsman's Eye that instantly reveals all medicinal applications of an object (medicine, tools, exam machines, chemical substances, etc). Techno-organic beings are also within its purview. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Life 2</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Purge Illness with Reach assigned to instant use. It manifests as tears that can be stored for later use, but can only cure one Illness at a time. It can also permanently cure transplant rejection of a specified cause. If used on a being successfully analyzed on the previous turn with the first Attainment, it bypasses the disease's Withstand rating (like tailoring the treatment to their needs).</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Matter 2</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Gardener can a specify a medicinal goal (cure a disease, find a given herb, perform an operation, find a blood donor, find the patient's dossier, etc) and this will highlight everything organic, inorganic and techno-organic that is relevant to that goal, but not why. It will also highlight up to [Matter] medical supplies the Gardeners specify, making them great field medics and able to quickly take stock of supplies wherever they are.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Life 3</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Their signature fleshcrafting ability. A Life variation of Shaping with Reach assigned to instant use and sensory range. It can be used to graft parts from one being to another. Changes are permanent yet still subject to the rules of the Fallen World. In other words, incompatible parts will require the second Attainment to stop the body's rejection of them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">It can be used instantly to mold eyes shut, close mouths, bind legs to one another or for improvising &quot;handcuffs&quot;, pull organs from the person, etc. Withstood by Stamina.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Transplanting limbs, organs and so on requires extended Intelligence + Medicine rolls, but incompatible ones suffer from transplant rejection. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">It can also be used to replicate the voice and/or appearance of a being of the same species, or to alter one's own, using an extended Intelligence + Crafts roll, but it cannot affect Size. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Matter 3</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">A version of Shaping with Reach assigned to instant use and altering solids. If used to create medical equipment or prosthetics, it reduces the number of successes needed by [Matter]. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">It can also be used to integrate mechanical augmentations and prosthetics into a living beings using extended Intelligence + Medicine rolls. Fullmetal Alchemist style automail and Adam Jensen style augmentations are all possible if they have the components ready.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Many determined fleshcrafters use this in the hunt of cryptids with valuable organs, ripping walls and barriers open with their bare hands.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Life 4</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">A Gardener must be able to go anywhere to find a new remedy or heal their patients. This acts as Transform Life with Reach assigned to instant use and advanced duration, creating up to [Life] transformations. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Gardeners normally keep this effect active whenever they can, altering the properties of cell division to create new cells ever closer to their peak years, granting them eternal youth and an ability to remain in active duty indefinitely.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Matter 4</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Gardener becomes able to transform their limbs into bio-technological medicinal tools (look up the Shapers of the Yuuzhan Vong for a good representation of how this looks). This allows them to receive a bonus of [Matter] to any Medicine rolls for the duration. Furthermore, they can take an extended Intelligence + Medicine roll to degrade up to [Matter] points of damage of their choice, one per success. Lethal becomes Bashing and Bashing is fully healed. Attempting to degrade Aggravated damage requires spending a point of mana. Reach is assigned to instant use and advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Life 5</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Transform life costing one mana and one Willpower point, requiring a scene of preparation to activate. It allows up to [Life] characteristics to be added, has a Lasting effect and allows them to be inherited. When used on a being the Gardener personally fleshcrafted, they can allocate Potency instead to allow one of those changes to be passed down, at a ratio of one point per change. Plants, animals and techno-organic beings are all valid targets for this Attainment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Matter 5</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Forge Masters may be the virtuosos of Perfected Metals, but the Gardeners of Gilgamesh are the masters of Perfected Medicine. This is a variation of Hone The Perfected Form, costing a point of Mana, with Reach assigned to instant use and making the effect Lasting. It allows the Gardener to suppress the negative or positive medicinal effects of a substance. A chemo treatment can be made to have no negative effects, alcohol can be perfected to leave a pleasantly drunk sensation without dulling the senses or attacking the liver, unhealthy food can be made to cause no harm and drugs can be stripped of side effects, but it cannot stop a scalpel from cutting.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">With conjunctional Forces 3, radioactive materials can also be affected, creating radiation therapies with no side effects, X-rays that will not endanger the internal organs, etc.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Remember, nothing says &quot;Destroy the followers of the Lie&quot; like a hand made army. I am sure those rumors of how the Legacy first disappeared when they lost control of their creations and were wiped out in a tide of horror are probably just Guardian propaganda.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T18:20:46-08:00","id":1287784,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d be interested in reviewing it, but start a new topic instead of hijacking this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T06:35:44-08:00","id":1288588,"title":"","content":"Ok, bringing this back into focus, I'm not sold on the informed condition for the first Death attainment, Informed works best as a one time use condition, I mean you could take it like that if you want, but for something like this I think we can go for a custom made condition. Took a page out of werewolves Siskur-Dah condition for this though.<br /> <br /> <b>Sanctioned<br /> (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> Your character has been contracted by the Nizari and now has a mission to assassinate one person, for the duration of his mission, he gains bonus dice equal to the Death's arcanum mastery of the contracting mage for all actions that involve carrying his mission or they can be used to impose a penalty to anyone that would try to stop him from completing his mission this is chosen when taking the condition, on the other hand, any action that is not working towards advancing his mission suffers a this bonus as penalty. For Sleepers an Sleepwalkers, this is always a breaking point with a -3 penalty as you are setting yourself to commit murder (normal penalty would -5 for premeditated murder), Awakened mages can become inured to this using the normal methods but otherwise count this as an act of hubris on the understanding level.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Completing their mission, destroying the contract writ.<br /> <br /> <b>Beats:</b> Any exceptional success carrying on their mission grants a beat.<br /> <br /> Too crazy or just enough crazy? as for inuring, it would make sense that mages of the Nizari would make an Assassin's Masque where they are inured to the act of murder under certain circumstances. I'm not a fan of just inuring the act of murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T08:47:25-08:00","id":1288606,"title":"","content":"I looks a bit too potent for an Initiation level ability. Remember this is the 1st Attainment, yet its giving a Perfecting bonus and Fraying penalties. So if you mix the penalty of this Attainment with the one from the reverse Isolation, it does escalate its power by a good amount, at least making it powerful enough to require Conditions and boons to fight it. It needs to be useful and something you would want to prepare often, but not so much as to compete with the higher Attainments.<br /> <br /> I like the Connected custom condition Mrmdubois suggested:<br /> <br /> +2 to all mundane actions involving eliminating the target. It can also be resolved to upgrade a mundane action to an Exceptional Success. Lasts as long as the Attainment does, in other words Advanced Duration, which means master Nizari having up to a year to kill the target , ones with Death 2 having an entire day, Death 3 having a week, which is a pretty generous time between casts.<br /> <br /> it gives a really useful benefit while also allowing for a thematic resolution with the finishing blow. I am also a fan of the conjunctional Force components Eleizel came up with, giving the Nizari more flexibility.<br /> <br /> As for the Wisdom loss, you can see the contract as an extension of Legacy Wisdom. With it, the Nizari who crafted it can avoid the Act of Hubris, because he confirmed his sacred duty through the ritual. But it only works for that Nizari, other Nizari who did not craft their own writs are not empowered with the authority to carry out the execution. So destroying it might make more Wise Nizari withdraw, giving the target a bit of breathing room. But the cabal mates do not get the benefit, they are empowered to aid in the task, but have not been deputized to become divine executioners like the Legacy members. This means that there is an incentive for the Nizari to strike the finishing blow or Guardians with the proper Masques (or those entrusted by the Order with using Masques wisely), which resonates with their role as the police of the Awakened. Its also an idea that comes from my wish to make them self contained, give them the assassin starter kit and they are good to go, without needing to spend 4XP on an additional merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-16-2019, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T09:48:07-08:00","id":1288627,"title":"","content":"That makes sense, I though of it like that to make it grow as the mage grows, initiates get a nice bonus but masters are truly fearsome killers, I mean it is tied to mastery of the death arcanum, but I see your point too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:42:03-08:00","id":1291617,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Prerequisites:</span></b><br /> ok, what do you think of it like this:<br /> <br /> Oh before that, disclaimer, I know this is full of all kind of holes everywhere when it comes to the background and the doctrine, a little help refining that would be appreaciated.<br /> <br /> Also credit where credit is due, kudos and thanks to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\">KaiserAfini</a> for coming up with the attaiments. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Legacy: The Nizari</b></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Origins</b></span> <span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Parentage</b></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Path:</span></b> Mastigos</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Order:</span></b> Guardian of the Veil</span></span></span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Concept:</span></b> Assassins</span></span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Appearance: </span></b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Nizari </span></span></span>are encouraged to not make many waves, in their mundane lives they could be just about anybody, they many faces and backgrounds, quite a few of those are actually fabricated, they make heavy use of their masques to have several background ready for what a job would require. <br /> <br /> They only recruit from members of the order, those that show a great level of dedicaion and self sacrifice draw their attention and the very exigences from the order cull those that wouldn't be a good fit.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Background:</span> </b>The Nizari Fidai are what the old order of assassins was called, dated back to the 11th century days they were born in what is now the ruined Alamut fortress on the South Caspian province of Gilan near the Rudbar region in Iran, lead by a mystierious &quot;Old man of the mountain&quot; they were a political and religious faction of Shia Islam, or so history would have you believe, in reality they were a sect of Guardians that during their time used the political and religious turmoil of the era to further their secret agenda.<br /> <br /> Much of the legacy's past was lost with the destruction of their forstresses and the burning of the library of Alamut, when they were invaded by the Mongol Empire during the invasion of Khwarism or so they would have you believe in reality they orchestated their own fall to cover the legacy in another layer of secrecy and so they could spread their numbers further accross the world, somethings are commonly known about the order though, it's founder was a Guardian Epoch of the Mastgos Path, Hassan-i Sabbah responsible for the widespread nature on the middle east, though only a limited group of Nizari were actually awakened members of the legacy. He saw and suffered under the regime of the Seers of the Throne that manipulated events to steal the reign of the Caliph orchestating a coup and putting one of their own in the throne, captured for a time he took the opportnity to meditate and plan in his prison waiting and bidding his time untilt the moment was right to act, he was changed by the experience and in his very soul he rejected the Hubris of the Seers, change as he was he founded his movement taking over the fortress of Alamut and spreading from there. He used an army of sleepers to combat the influence of the Seers of the Throne using asymmetrical and psychological warfare and surgical strikes particulary their assassinations of key individuals.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">And for the better part of three centuries they were a force to be reckon with, having succefully assassinated key figures across their early history, two known Caliphs, many viziers, sultans and crusader leaders.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nowadays the legacy no longer subscribes to a particular set of beliefs religious or otherwise, you can see traces of them among the history of the world, the cold war was basically their playground, in more modern settings they can be easily found as part of black ops teams in any miliatry or as hitmen among the criminal underworld, some venerate the Santa Muerte in the mexicans cartels, so work in any of the soup letter intelligence agencies across the world, their background may vary, though their purpose and MO remain the same.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <span style=\"color:#3366ff\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Prerequisites: </span></b></span>Gnosis 2, Death 2, Status 2 Guardian of the Veil and at least one mastered Masque.</span></span></span><ul><li><b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Thesis:</span></b> It is the nature of the Diamond Wheel to advance, refining all souls while flattening the trail for the arrival the Hieromagus, who shall redeem all sins and reclaim the Imperium Mysteriorum for mankind. The Exarchs would chain its movements so this does not come to pass.<br /> <br /> But there is one Truth they forget: All things contain shatterpoints, precise locations that can be stricken to utterly destroy them. So too does destiny, for a simple phrase or speech can change the course of history or an army can be rendered ineffective by the death of few key figures. For the chosen few, even the fetters of the Tyrants can become evident. See the chains of the lie, become the blade that will sever its weakest link and allow the Diamond Wheel to turn unhindered.</li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Organization: </span></b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The unifying doctrine of the Nizari is their dedication to their cause, what is their cause changes from Caucus from Caucus, but some things remain constant, they are never the ones leading, they can hold authority over others, but never are they the leader or heriarchs on the concilium, they are followers, very dedicated followers, but just followers in the end, if such would take such lofty ambision for himself it better be on a temporary manner and setting the stage for a proper leader to replace him one way or another or he would see himself eventually culled from the ranks of the Legacy. No, the Nizari themselves don't rule, they are the power behind the throne others are the sword and shield of the Pentacle orders, the Nizari are happy to be their silent blade in the night.<br /> <br /> There is a reason for this though, a Nizari for the most part try to avoid the trappings of hubris and one of the easier ones to fall comes from sitting in positions of power so they limit themselves this way, there is also the belief that they are just paving their mythical messiah, the Heriomage who they will submit under for judegement of their dedication to its cause, the unfaithful would be cast aside while the steadfast and loyal will be recieved with open arms, finally having sanction from above actually empowers them in their missions allowing them to carry out their assassinations wihtout risking their wisdom in the act.<br /> <br /> They work within the order, they are Guardians of the Veil first and they follow the orders traditions and practices, they make it to the rank os Susceptors most of the time where they settle down, there are occassional grand masters in the legacy but their focus is on recruitment and management of the order members in the local caucus under the vigilant eye of the Epoch, they aren't really numerous as they not many have the temperament to dedicate themselves to the levels that the Nizari do.</span></span></span></li> <li><b>Initiation: </b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Nizari ritual of initiation is rather straightfoward but by not mean easy, quite the contrary, in fact the prospective Nizari is tested against an impossible task, this test the initiate in their resourcefulness and dedication, he's pretty much set out to fail in a controled scenario, most commonly he is set up against a disguised member of the legacy willing to play the part of a mark, though to prevent misshaps he is not told to kill his target, just to capture it alive wich normaly adds another layer of difficulty to the task as he's told to do it discreetly and without being caught on the act. The mark is prepared for this and stacks the deck against the prospective new member, occasionaly with his mentor help in a way that is made sure to mess up his plan, how he reacts and adapts under this circumstances makes or breaks the prospective Nizari, though if he actually succeeds against all odds he's quickly inducted into the Legacy. </span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Ruling Arcana</span></b></span><br /> Death<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#cccccc\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><b><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Optional Arcana</span></span></b></b></span></span><br /> Space<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Yantras</span></b></span><br /> Detailed files about a Mark (+1), Having been Sanctioned to act by a superior (+2), Tool or weapons of assassination (+1), Using stimulants to keep focused (+1, +2 if a negative condition is caused), While in the presence of their mark and undetected (+1)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\"><b><span style=\"color:#3366ff\">Oblations</span></b></span><br /> Studying a target's life, a long session of planning a hit, Shadowing a target, Infiltrating a target's social group, meditatiing on why the target needs to die, announcing the intent to kill the target while explaining why he is going to die.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Attainments</span></b> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">First Attainment: Deadly Sanction</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 1</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spend a scene building a writ of sanctioned assassination for the target, requiring a representational yantra and some data on them. This grants the assassin and any that have signed their names on the writ the Sanctioned condition, useable only for actions to kill the target. If the writ is destroyed, the Condition goes away.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b>Sanctioned:</b></span> The character enjoys a <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">+2 </span></span>to all mundane actions involving eliminating the target. It can also be resolved to upgrade a mundane action to an Exceptional Success. Lasts as long as the Attainment does, which means master Nizari having up to a year to kill the target , ones with Death 2 having an entire day, Death 3 having a week, this condition also prevents member of the Legacy from commiting an sin against Wisdom when he set's up to kill his target, but only when it comes to direct actions against his target or targets, killing allies, retainers or bystanders still counts as an Act of Hubris, non legacy members however don't benefit from this.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b>Space 1</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">After a scene of meditating on the mission, your divine mandate wards you from interference. This applies an inverse variation of Isolation upon yourself or an ally, giving the penalty to any Unsanctioned who try to interact with the beneficiary. You can also apply normal Isolation on a target. Any Sanctioned can interact with them normally, but its a two way street.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Second Attainment: Deadly Silence/Reaching Hands</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 2</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Renders a target (the Nizari, the victim, the murder weapon, etc) completely silent. Reach is assigned to instant use and advanced duration.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b>Space 2</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">All of your Legacy Attainments can now be used with Sympathetic Range.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Third Attainment: Death's Touch/Hidden Armory</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 3</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">As the Decay spell with [Death] potency and Reach assigned to instant use and Structural damage.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b>Space 3</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Physics tells us that no two objects can occupy the same space, but such things cannot get in the way of an assassin's divine mission. After a scene of preparing to go out on the field, they can link objects together, allowing one to exist at a time while the other is in a &quot;pocket dimension&quot;. Swapping between them is a reflexive action. So a pen can be used to smuggle a gun in, a ring can become a knife or a trusted friend can unknowingly be a time bomb. Up to [Space] pairs of objects can be linked at a time.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Fourth Attainment: Mantle of Darkness/Garrote of the Heart</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 4</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This attainment combines Deepen Shadows and Without a Trace that allows up to 5 Sanctioned see normally within the shadows, and to be affected by Without a Trace for the Duration. Any Unsanctioned who use supernatural effects to try see within provoke a Clash of Wills, earning [Death] automatic successes for the assassin. Reach are spent on Instant Use, Advanced Scale and Advanced Duration.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b>Space 4</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Twists the nature of sympathetic links, but not the strength. So a person's link to their spouse could go from &quot;love&quot; to &quot;violent repulsion&quot;. Had you borrowed the &quot;love&quot; link, you could alter it to &quot;trusted confidant&quot;. Or even alter the link one has to a pet from &quot;loyal friend&quot; to &quot;pathological fear&quot;. Reach is assigned to instant use and advanced duration.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\">Fifth Attainment: Supernal Death/Umbral Roads</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Prerequisite: </span></span></b>Death 5</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spend a mana to kill all Unsanctioned supernatural effects in the area Withstood by their potency rating. Reach is used on instant use and mana is spent on activating Everywhere.</span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><b><span style=\"color:#3333ff\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif\">Optional Arcana: </span></span></b></span></b>Space 5</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">As the Teleportation spell with Reach assigned to instant use.</span></span></span></span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 02-26-2019, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:18:52-08:00","id":1291985,"title":"","content":"It appears that you already have the doctrine in the writeup, it just needs to be organized. This is a format I like to use, borrowed from the 2ed Legacies thread: <br /> <br /> <b>Origins:</b><br /> <br /> Parentage: Path and Order they are from<br /> <br /> Background: How they came to be, history<br /> <br /> Appearances: How do they normally dress ? How do they normally behave? What impression do they give?<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> <br /> Prerequisites: You have this done, skill and Arcana needed to be initiated <br /> <br /> Initiation: What test, ritual or simular observance is required to become a full fledged member ?<br /> <br /> Organization: How is the Legacy structured in the present day ? How do they communicate ? Do they have any kind of leadership ? Are they lead by seniority or do they use a different system, if any ?<br /> <br /> Theory: An elevator pitch to tell a prospective member or an outsider what this Legacy is all about.<br /> <br /> The Magic part looks pretty solid. For yantras, it could be interesting to add one for having a terrified target, one for them being intoxicated (drunk, poisoned, groggy with sleep, etc) and one for them being unaware of your presence.<br /> <br /> For oblations, how about anonymously terrifying a target with their guilt ? For example, if they killed someone's wife for the Exarchs and buried the body in the woods, the Nizari would send her wedding ring by mail. Or they could make an accusatory call while masking their voice, or send a letter made of magazine clippings, or even something akin to the horse head scene from the Godfather. So long as it can be justified as requiring a scene to prepare or execute, it counts.<br /> <br /> If Attainment names are still open for suggestions, perhaps Ubral Roads could suit the teleportation one and maybe Garrote of the Heart for the one that alters sympathetic connections.<br /> <br /> I think it might also be worth adding to the first Attainment that the Nizari who created the writ does not commit an Act of Hubris when killing the specified target, that info is currently found in their history. If the Nizari kills any henchman, bystanders or the like, they will have to roll Wisdom. Sanctioned non-Legacy members roll Wisdom as normal for all kills, even the target (so the Nizari is incentivized to strike the finishing blow).<br /> <br /> For Theory, here is an idea, let me know if it matches the tone you are going for:<br /> <br /> It is the nature of the Diamond Wheel to advance, refining all souls while flattening the trail for the arrival the Hieromagus, who shall redeem all sins and reclaim the Imperium Mysteriorum for mankind. The Exarchs would chain its movements so this does not come to pass.<br /> <br /> But there is one Truth they forget: All things contain shatterpoints, precise locations that can be stricken to utterly destroy them. So too does destiny, for a simple phrase or speech can change the course of history or an army can be rendered ineffective by the death of few key figures. For the chosen few, even the fetters of the Tyrants can become evident. See the chains of the lie, become the blade that will sever its weakest link and allow the Diamond Wheel to turn unhindered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-26-2019, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T18:42:48-08:00","id":1292324,"title":"","content":"Loved the Theory and added it already, also adde an apperance (sort of), expanded a bit more on their history and organization and added an initiation.<br /> <br /> Also my ST vetoed the Death 5 attainment, saying that the ability to cancel all supernatural effecfts is too much, trying to come up with a replacement, we could say it kills one single effect per activation I guess, or I came up with something.<br /> <br /> Weight of Souls or Death's Rejection<br /> Death 5<br /> The Nizari dedication carries them on even in the face of death, with this attaiment he prepares a ritual using a strong sympathy yantra to the target he creates a link with his victim, if the Nizari mage dies before killing his target his soul doens't depart inmediatly but lingers back to his body for a time (an hour maybe?) (if there is a body to return to and it isn't too damaged) if in that time he can reach his target he may kill him to make him trade his life with his own.<br /> <br /> that was inspired a bit from Deny the Reaper<br /> <br /> Also found some inspiration material from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serenity_(2005_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Serenity Film</a>, in particular The Operative and his quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 02-26-2019, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T05:35:53-08:00","id":1292463,"title":"","content":"Cool, glad you liked it. The writeup is looking pretty good. <br /> <br /> Did your GM think the last Death Attainment was able to cancel thing like other Attainments, Mage Armors or Werewolf Gift ? Because that would be insane. I meant more along the lines of leveraging the fact that Unmaking practices are &quot;save or die&quot; to say that any Unsactioned spells inside the area with Potency less than [Death] simply get dispelled.<br /> <br /> That being said, I like your new Attainment a lot more. How about making it so the Nizari can spend a point of mana when making the writ to imbue it with this ability? If they die, the sympathetic link is formed and they get the ghost form. Reach is spent on Advanced Duration, in other words, this lasts a year at most.<br /> <br /> The ghost is a Rank 2 ghost in Twilight, with max stats for this level and Numina determined when this Attainment is obtained and Influence 2: Killing.<br /> <br /> They spend mana instead of Essence and regain it close to the writ, just like normal ghosts. Everything else is per ghost rules, so they must also spend a point per day to remain active. But if the writ gets destroyed, so does the Nizari. If the target dies before it expires, the writ is consumed and the Nizari is revived where it was.<br /> <br /> This form could have 2 more peculiar abilities. The first is that it can jump to any sympathetically connection they have by spending a point of mana. The second is that the writ constantly whispers, in ghostly voices, everything the Nizari sees. Does this draw a very uncomfortable parallel to the Grigori? Yes it does. It also makes you question what actually happened in the Alamut and why they chose to break away from the old ways, which can be fun plot hooks for your GM to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-27-2019, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T17:13:36-08:00","id":1292648,"title":"","content":"Got to ask, what are the Grigory? where can I find them to read about it?<br /> <br /> Also, what about something like this?<ul><li>The Nizari dedication carries them on even in the face of death, with this attaiment he spends 1 mana while creating the writ, this creates a stronger connection between the Nizari and his target, if the Nizari mage dies before killing his target his soul doens't depart inmediatly but lingers back to the writ after a time (an hour maybe?) as a Rank 2 ghost in twilight with maximun stats for this level, numina determinated when this attainment is obtained, Influences: Killing, mana instead of essence and finally the ability to jump between sympathetic connections by spending 1 point of mana.<br /> <br /> The writ becomes the Nizari ghosts anchor to this world if it is destroyed the Nizari souls departs (He can also be destroyed like a normal ghost like this), but if the target dies before the writ expires or is destroyed the writ is consumed and Nizari revives where it is.<br /> <br /> The writ gains a peculiarity however, it starts to whisper in ghostly voices everything that the Nizari sees. (Reach is used for Advanced Duration)</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:13:59-08:00","id":1292665,"title":"","content":"The Grigori are the servitors of the Seers loyal to Panopticon. You can find them in the Seers book and probably have a brief mention in the 2e core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T10:57:47-08:00","id":1292813,"title":"","content":"That looks pretty spot on.<br /> <br /> So to explain it a bit, the Seers can access some exclusive Artifacts, which come from who knows where, yet show up disturbingly often, at least by Artifact standards. A signature one is the Profane Urim. Wrap it on a target and you get to posses them and have a Connected sympathetic link to them. <br /> <br /> But Panopticon get a special variation. You wrap it around a target and it forces them into Twilight as a ghost, with the Urim acting as an Anchor. This is a torturous existence, the shrowd bind and constrains them, eyes pop up all around them and they cannot return to their body, which the Artifact sustains. These beings are called Grigori.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, a Grigori is a Rank 2 ghost with Influence 2: Watching. It can move to any sympathetic connections they have, making that point a new &quot;Anchor&quot;. They see all around them and the body is forced to report everything they perceive, they also cannot disobey the user. So if you combine that with Borrow Threads and the Prelacy of Vision, it becomes an amazing spying tool or an invisible hitman.<br /> <br /> So just remove the person from the Urim and they are fine, right ? Nope, that kills them, which might be better than the alternative. And that is the &quot;nicest&quot; transformation Seers use to create servants. The Seers book does an outstanding job of fleshing them out as villains, I highly recommend it.<br /> <br /> But anyway, the fifth Attainment could be seen as a result of a Seer infiltrator trying to replicate Grigori for their own Ministry, or even create their own improved version. Or it could be the result of the Guardians trying to copy such convenient abilities and crossing the Moral Event Horizon, causing the Diamond to interfere or the Legacy to split. Maybe its all the above. Its left open to leave the GM with a fun plot hook to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-28-2019, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T06:41:02-07:00","id":1297496,"title":"","content":"So my GM liked the new attainment and approved the legacy for play, so Yay success! Also, I put a name for the modified Isolation attainment, now it's called Detached Presence.<br /> <br /> Thanks everybody for helping out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}